<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tigernán Ua Ruairc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1172">1172</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Tigernan Ua Ruairc</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tigernán Ua Ruairc (died 1172) was king of Breifne for nearly fifty years and one of the most powerful Irish rulers of the 12th century. The abduction of his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derbforgaill">Derbforgaill</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a> in 1152 fed a long feud, and he helped drive Diarmait into exile in 1166, which led to the Anglo-Norman invasion. He was killed in 1172 at a parley with Hugh de Lacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tigernan-ua-ruairc.jpg" alt="Tigernán Ua Ruairc" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Erakis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ireland900.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
